-- title:
--   Moving a cusp-centred place to a good point (q=3)
-- statement:
--   Notation. $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ is `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`; for a valuation subring $A$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ write $k_A$ for its residue field. Put $\mathcal F=$ `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the subfield of the Laurent series over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ generated over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ by the coefficientwise image of the full level-$M'$ modular function field; $\mathcal F_C=$ `modularFunctionFieldC k_A M'`, generated over $k_A$ by `jqModC` and its $M'$-expansion; $F=$ `fieldBar q M'`, the subfield of the Laurent series over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the function field of $X_H(q^2M')$ for $H=$ `levelH q M'`, the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$; and $F_C=$ `xHFunctionFieldC k_A (q^2*M') (levelH q M')`. A `Place K F` is a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$, distinct from $F$, whose ideals are principal; it is rational when $K$ surjects onto its residue field, and `evalAt` returns the element of $K$ representing the residue of an integral element (and $0$ otherwise). `ssJSet q Ω` is the set of $j\in\Omega$ such that every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with invariant $j$ has no nonzero point killed by $q$.
--
--   Data and base hypotheses. Let $q$ be a prime with $q=3$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$ (`LiesOverPrime`). Let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathcal F_C$ over $k_A$, required by `hW` to be exactly the set `ssPlaces q M' k_A` of supersingular places: those $w$ that are rational, are affine geometric places, and satisfy $w(\mathrm{jGeomGen})\in$ `ssJSet q k_A`. The hypothesis `hle` asserts $\mathcal F\subseteq F$. Let $R_0$ be a `ConstantReduction` of $\mathcal F$ to $\mathcal F_C$ over $A$: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ of $\mathcal F$ whose intersection with $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ is $A$, a surjective residue homomorphism onto $\mathcal F_C$ with kernel the maximal ideal and compatible with $A\to k_A$, the property that every nonzero element can be scaled by a constant into the integers with nonzero residue, together with a map on places preserving degrees and compatible with divisors under `Finsupp.mapDomain`. The hypothesis `hR₀` requires: for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose image over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $\mathcal F$, that image lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its residue, read as a Laurent series over $k_A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Let $\zeta$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ (`Idx q`), and let $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ be a family of valuation subrings of $F$ indexed by the projective line $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$ and $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ a family indexed by $W$.
--
--   Igusa group (`hIg_inf`, `hIg`, `hIg_inj`, `hIg_perm`). The ring at the point $\infty=[1:0]$ (`lineInfty q`) is described by: $f\in O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ if and only if there are Laurent series $x,y$ with coefficients in $A$ such that the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ is nonzero and $f\cdot y=x$ in the Laurent series over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$. For every line $\ell$ there is $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ whose reduction `redQ q γ` carries $\infty$ to $\ell$ and with $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ the preimage of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ under `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`. The map $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ is injective. For every primitive root $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ there is a permutation $\sigma$ of $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$ with $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ pulled back along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` equal to $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\sigma\ell)$ for all $\ell$.
--
--   Supersingular group (`hSS_A`, `hSS_over`, `hSS_fix`, `hSS_tr`). For each $s\in W$ and $x\in\bar{\mathbb Q}$, the image of $x$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ exactly when $x\in A$. For each $s\in W$ and each $f\in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ whose order is non-negative at every place of $\mathcal F$ over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ at which the $j$-expansion element `coeffEmb Q̄ jq` has non-negative order: if the $R_0$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$, then the image of $f$ in $F$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$, and for every $a\in A$ whose residue equals the value of $s$ at that $R_0$-residue, the difference of the image of $f$ and $a$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and in its maximal ideal. Each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ is its own preimage under `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for all $\zeta'$ and all $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$. Finally, for each $s$ there is $t\in O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ such that $t-a$ is a unit of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ for every $a\in A$.
--
--   Prolongation and arithmetic base. Let $R$ be a `RegularProlongation` of $F$ to $F_C$ over $A$ (the same data as a constant reduction, without the place map, degree and divisor clauses), with $R.\mathrm{integers}=O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$, and let `hR₀O` require that $f\in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ if and only if the image of $f$ in $F$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$. Let $\pi\in A$ satisfy $\pi^{q^2-1}=q$. Let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\bar{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ an element of $A$, such that $A\cap k_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is a henselian local ring, and has algebraically closed residue field; and let `hκ` require that every $a\in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some element of $k_0$ lying in $A$. Let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell\ge 3$, $\ell\ne q$, $\ell\nmid M'$, let $\zeta_0\in k_0$ be a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity, and let $\varpi_t\in k_0$ lie in $A$ and satisfy $\varpi_t^{q^2-1}=q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. Let $K_1$ be a finite extension of $k_0$ inside $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ and $A_1$ a valuation subring of $K_1$ consisting exactly of the elements of $K_1$ lying in $A$, which is a henselian discrete valuation ring.
--
--   Conclusion. Regard $F$ as a $k_0$-algebra through $\bar{\mathbb Q}$. Let $F_0$ be an intermediate field of $F/k_0$ satisfying the form group: (i) the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ is all of $F$; (ii) $F_0$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for every $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; (iii) for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$, every $m$, every $c:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to\bar{\mathbb Q}$ and every $a:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to F$ with all $a_i$ in the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$, if $c$ is linearly independent over $K'$ and $\sum_i c_i a_i=0$ then all $a_i=0$; (iv) every element of $F$ whose underlying Laurent series has rational coefficients (lies in the range of `coeffEmb`) belongs to $F_0$. Write $T_1$ for the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield of $F$ generated by the image of $K_1$. Let $T_1$ carry an $A_1$-algebra structure whose structure map is the inclusion $K_1\subseteq\bar{\mathbb Q}\to F$, and let $j_1\in T_1$ be nonzero and equal, in $F$, to the image under `IntermediateField.inclusion hle` of the element `coeffEmb Q̄ jq` of $\mathcal F$. Let $\mathfrak X=$ `TwoChartIntegralModel A₁ T₁ j₁`, the pushout of the two affine charts $\mathrm{Spec}$ of `chartAlgFin` (the elements of $T_1$ integral over $A_1[j_1]$) and $\mathrm{Spec}$ of `chartAlgInf` (integral over $A_1[j_1^{-1}]$), with the canonical morphisms `ιFin`, `ιInf` and the structure morphism `toBase` to $\mathrm{Spec}\,A_1$.
--
--   The statement introduces the following abbreviations. For $x\in\mathfrak X$ and $f\in T_1$: `InStalk x f` holds when for every prime $y$ of `chartAlgFin` mapping to $x$ under `ιFin` there are $g,h$ in `chartAlgFin` with $h\notin y$ and $f\cdot h=g$, and likewise for `chartAlgInf` and `ιInf`; `InMax x f` is the same with the additional requirement $g\in y$. For a place $P$ of $F$ over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$, `Centred P x` holds when $P$ is rational and every $f$ with `InStalk x f` lies in the valuation subring of $P$, has $P$-value in $A$, and this value has $A$-valuation $<1$ precisely when `InMax x f`. `GoodPt x` is the conjunction of: `toBase` sends $x$ to the closed point of $\mathrm{Spec}\,A_1$; every $y$ with $x\rightsquigarrow y$ equals $x$; for every $y$ over $x$ in the finite chart, every element of `chartAlgFin` whose image in $F$ is a non-unit of $R.\mathrm{integers}$ lies in $y$; the same for the chart at infinity; and for every $y$ over $x$ in the finite chart, every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from `chartAlgFin` to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j_1)$ does not lie in `ssJSet q Ω`. Two further abbreviations are introduced and do not occur in the final assertion: `Reads x Q`, for a place $Q$ of $F_C$, requiring every $f$ with `InStalk x f` to lie in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ with $R$-residue in the valuation subring of $Q$, that residue being a non-unit there exactly when `InMax x f`; and `OffBranch x`, requiring for every line $\ell\ne\infty$ and every $y$ over $x$ in either chart an element of the corresponding chart algebra whose image in $F$ is a non-unit of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ and which does not lie in $y$.
--
--   The assertion is then: for every place $P$ of $F$ over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ and every point $x$ of $\mathfrak X$ such that `Centred P x` holds and $x$ is not in the image of the base map of `ιFin`, there exist $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and a point $x'$ of $\mathfrak X$ such that `GoodPt x'` holds and `Centred (levelAutBar q M' ζ γ • P) x'` holds, the place $P$ being translated by the level automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`.
--
--   This is the $q = 3$ case of the cusp-moving step in the study of the two-chart integral model of the full level-$q^2M'$ modular curve over a henselian discrete valuation ring $A_1$: a rational place centred at a point of the model lying outside the finite ($j$-integral) chart is carried by a level automorphism onto a place centred at a point of the special fibre which is closed, kills the non-units of the Igusa ring at infinity in both charts, and has non-supersingular $j$-invariant. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_levelAutBar_smul_centred_twoChartIntegralModel_of_forall_not_ssTube_of_eq_three`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_levelAutBar_smul_centred_twoChartIntegralModel_of_forall_not_ssTube_of_eq_three) in the construction of the semistable covering of the curve.
